  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/RaaghavC/open-worldline/zipball/wan22-action-fixed16-a100-v1",
  "body": "Original 947,712-parameter action adapter: a fresh sixteen-update CUDA training run on an A100 80 GB, using an attributed, frozen Wan2.2 TI2V-5B base. All sixteen paired updates completed in 260.465 seconds including model loading and verification. The independent retained-file audit passed. All 825 base parameter records remained unchanged; both initial native-versus-zero-adapter predictions were bit-exact.\n\nThis release contains no generated video from the trained adapter. It does not establish action control, visual quality, generalization, world memory, Genie 3 parity or a scientific breakthrough. Training uses eight windows from one original Atrium layout; only the initial shared-observation pair isolates different commands. A training loss is not a visual-quality metric.\n\nThe complete recovery contains 485 files totaling 616,066,326 bytes. Six independently hashed transport parts total 464,908,340 bytes. index.json pins every recovered file. It includes all 17 checkpoints, saved optimizer/RNG states, 32 training predictions, 16 gradient files, numerical comparisons, source copies and logs. Foundation weights and credentials are excluded.\n\nThe executed repository source is commit 099eeae6268da852b0acb580258e4c168f900520, retained in worldline-action-cuda-099eeae6268d.tar.gz. Four additional executed fixed16 source/test files and their nine-check CPU report are retained in the recovery and fixed16-preparation.tar.gz. The repository tag points to the publication context, not a claim that later documentation was executed. scripts.tar.gz retains the original cloud preparation scripts.\n\nThe unchanged internal worker limit was 900 seconds. A separate 720-second process-group limit with a 10-second kill grace preserved recovery time under the unchanged one-hour lease; it did not trigger. The instance was subsequently deleted, absence verified by both GET and complete list, and the temporary key revoked.\n\nSee LICENSE-NOTES.md and the included component licenses: original project code Apache-2.0, attributed Wan source Apache-2.0 with its notice, original Atrium scene/data CC0, capture code GPL-3.0-or-later. External foundation weights must be obtained separately under their own distribution terms.\n"
